  "trustHubTitle": "Trust & Privacy",
  "trustHubSubtitle": "Clear answers about how Lune protects your health data — security, cookies, accessibility, and more.",
  "trustHubLink": "Trust & Privacy Center",

  "trustLinkSecurity": "Security at Lune",
  "trustLinkSecuritySub": "Encryption, authentication, and how we protect your data",
  "trustLinkBodyData": "Your Body, Your Data",
  "trustLinkBodyDataSub": "You own your cycle data — we never sell it",
  "trustLinkDataEnds": "Your Data Ends With You",
  "trustLinkDataEndsSub": "Delete your account and cloud data anytime",
  "trustLinkFaq": "Privacy FAQ",
  "trustLinkFaqSub": "Common questions about privacy at Lune",
  "trustLinkCookies": "Cookie Policy",
  "trustLinkCookiesSub": "How we use local storage and website cookies",
  "trustLinkIp": "IP Address Use",
  "trustLinkIpSub": "Why we process IP addresses and what we don't do",
  "trustLinkAccessibility": "Accessibility",
  "trustLinkAccessibilitySub": "Our commitment to an inclusive experience",

  "trustSecurityTitle": "Security at Lune",
  "trustSecurityIntro": "Your health data deserves bank-grade care. Security is built into every layer of Lune — not added as an afterthought. This page explains how we protect your cycle logs, account, and optional cloud features in plain language.",
  "trustSecurityS1Title": "Encryption on your device",
  "trustSecurityS1Body": "Your cycle database is encrypted locally using AES-256 before it is stored on your phone. Symptom, mood, flow, and wellness entries live inside this protected store. Encryption keys are generated on your device and stored in Android Keystore or iOS Keychain — they never leave your device unprotected.",
  "trustSecurityS2Title": "Encrypted cloud sync (optional, Premium)",
  "trustSecurityS2Body": "Cloud backup is optional and requires Premium plus your explicit consent. When enabled, your cycle backup payload is encrypted on the device before upload and stored in your private Firebase account. We do not claim every Firestore profile field uses the same AES-256 scheme — the sensitive cycle payload itself is encrypted before it leaves your phone.",
  "trustSecurityS3Title": "Secure connections & app integrity",
  "trustSecurityS3Body": "All network traffic uses TLS encryption. Firebase App Check helps verify genuine app requests. You can sign in with email, Google, Apple, or continue as an anonymous guest — each method is handled through Firebase Authentication with industry-standard protections.",
  "trustSecurityS4Title": "No ads, no data brokers",
  "trustSecurityS4Body": "Lune does not show third-party ads and does not sell your personal or health data. We do not share your cycle data with advertisers, data brokers, employers, or insurers. Our revenue comes from optional Premium subscriptions, not from monetizing your health information.",
  "trustSecurityS5Title": "You control optional features",
  "trustSecurityS5Body": "AI chat (Google Gemini and DeepSeek), community, push notifications, and cloud sync are optional and require your consent. You can review and change these choices anytime in Privacy Center without affecting core local tracking.",
  "trustSecurityS6Title": "Crash reporting (Firebase Crashlytics)",
  "trustSecurityS6Body": "Lune uses Firebase Crashlytics to collect anonymized crash reports and basic diagnostic data when the app fails unexpectedly. This helps us fix bugs quickly. Crash reports do not include your cycle logs, wellness entries, or AI chat content.",
  "trustSecurityS7Title": "Cloud infrastructure",
  "trustSecurityS7Body": "Registered accounts, optional cloud backups, community content, and AI chat (for Premium users) run on Google Firebase — including Authentication, Firestore, Cloud Functions, Cloud Messaging, Hosting, App Check, and Crashlytics. Access to your data is restricted by Firebase security rules and your sign-in credentials.",
  "trustSecurityS8Title": "Stealth mode on your device",
  "trustSecurityS8Body": "Stealth mode disguises Lune as a calculator until you enter your PIN. This protects privacy on your phone if someone picks it up — it is a local lock only and does not encrypt data differently. You can enable or disable it in Privacy Center.",
  "trustSecurityS9Title": "Payment security",
  "trustSecurityS9Body": "Premium subscriptions on Android are processed by Google Play Billing. Lune never sees or stores your card number. Manage or cancel your subscription through your Google Play account settings.",
  "trustSecurityS10Title": "Android app permissions",
  "trustSecurityS10Body": "Lune requests only permissions needed for features you use: Internet (sign-in, optional cloud sync, AI, community), Notifications (optional cycle reminders), Google Play Billing (Premium), exact alarms and boot restart (reliable local reminders), and photos/media only when you choose to attach an image or set a profile photo. Android backup for app data is disabled (allowBackup=false) so cycle data is not copied to Google device backup by default.",

  "trustCookiesTitle": "Cookie & Storage Policy",
  "trustCookiesIntro": "Lune is a mobile app first. This page explains what is stored on your device, what our website keeps, and what we deliberately do not track. We believe clarity about storage is part of respecting your privacy.",
  "trustCookiesS1Title": "App local storage",
  "trustCookiesS1Body": "The Lune app stores your cycle logs, wellness entries, preferences, consent choices, and (if you are a guest) AI chat history on your device using encrypted local databases and secure storage. This is essential for offline tracking and fast daily logging.",
  "trustCookiesS2Title": "Website cookies",
  "trustCookiesS2Body": "Our website (lune-7d956.web.app) does not use advertising or tracking cookies. We may use essential technical storage — such as remembering your language choice on legal pages — so you do not have to re-select it every visit.",
  "trustCookiesS3Title": "No ad tracking",
  "trustCookiesS3Body": "We do not use third-party ad networks, cross-app trackers, or marketing pixels in the Lune app. Your health data is never used for targeted advertising, audience profiling, or retargeting campaigns.",
  "trustCookiesS4Title": "Managing storage",
  "trustCookiesS4Body": "You can clear local app data by uninstalling the app or deleting your account from Privacy Center. Exported backup files you save to your clipboard or elsewhere remain under your control — delete them when you no longer need them.",
  "trustCookiesS5Title": "Push notification tokens",
  "trustCookiesS5Body": "If you enable notifications, Firebase Cloud Messaging stores a device token so we can deliver cycle reminders and app updates you asked for. This token is used for delivery only — not for advertising or selling your identity to third parties.",
  "trustCookiesS6Title": "Community cache",
  "trustCookiesS6Body": "When you browse communities, posts and images may be cached temporarily on your device for smoother scrolling. This cache is part of normal app performance and is cleared when you uninstall the app or clear app data.",
  "trustCookiesS7Title": "Language & consent preferences",
  "trustCookiesS7Body": "Your language choice, Privacy Center consent toggles, and stealth-mode settings are saved locally so the app remembers your preferences between sessions. These settings stay on your device unless you sign in and sync account-level preferences.",
  "trustCookiesS8Title": "What we never store for ads",
  "trustCookiesS8Body": "We do not place ad cookies, social pixels, or behavioral tracking SDKs in Lune. We do not build marketing profiles from your cycle data, symptoms, moods, or AI conversations.",

  "trustIpTitle": "How We Use IP Addresses",
  "trustIpIntro": "When you use Lune or our website, your IP address may be processed by our infrastructure providers. This page explains why that happens, what we do not do with it, and the choices available to you.",
  "trustIpS1Title": "Why IP addresses are processed",
  "trustIpS1Body": "IP addresses help Firebase and our Cloud Functions deliver requests securely, route traffic to the correct server, and keep the service available. Without basic network metadata, cloud apps cannot function reliably.",
  "trustIpS2Title": "What we do not do",
  "trustIpS2Body": "We do not sell IP addresses, use them for advertising profiles, or attempt to determine your precise physical location from your IP alone. Your IP is not shared with data brokers or ad networks.",
  "trustIpS3Title": "Retention",
  "trustIpS3Body": "IP addresses in server and hosting logs are kept only as long as needed for security, abuse prevention, and troubleshooting. They are then rotated or deleted according to Firebase and Google Cloud retention policies.",
  "trustIpS4Title": "Your choices",
  "trustIpS4Body": "Using a VPN is your choice — we do not penalize VPN users. Deleting your account removes your profile and associated cloud content from our servers. For full details, see our Privacy Policy.",
  "trustIpS5Title": "Rate limits & abuse prevention",
  "trustIpS5Body": "We apply server-side rate limits on AI chat and community actions to prevent spam and protect all users. IP addresses and authenticated account IDs may be used together to detect abusive patterns — never to profile you for marketing.",
  "trustIpS6Title": "Where data may be processed",
  "trustIpS6Body": "Firebase and our AI providers may process requests in the United States and other regions where Google and DeepSeek operate data centers. This is standard for cloud-hosted health apps with optional sync.",
  "trustIpS7Title": "Legal requests",
  "trustIpS7Body": "We may disclose information — which could include IP-related server logs — only when required by valid legal process and to the minimum extent the law demands. We do not voluntarily share cycle health data with authorities.",
  "trustIpS8Title": "VPNs and privacy tools",
  "trustIpS8Body": "If you use a VPN, your visible IP may differ from your physical region. Lune does not block VPN connections. Some Firebase security checks may still apply to protect accounts from takeover attempts.",

  "trustFaqTitle": "Privacy FAQ",
  "trustFaqIntro": "Answers to the questions we hear most about privacy, security, and how Lune handles your cycle data. If you do not find your answer here, contact us anytime.",
  "trustFaqQ1": "Who can see my cycle data?",
  "trustFaqA1": "Only you. By default, your cycle data stays on your device in an encrypted local database. If you enable Premium cloud backup, encrypted copies are stored in your private Firebase account. We do not share cycle data with other users unless you explicitly post in community features.",
  "trustFaqQ2": "Does Lune sell my data?",
  "trustFaqA2": "No. We never sell your personal or health data. Lune is funded through optional Premium subscriptions processed by Google Play — not through advertising or data brokerage.",
  "trustFaqQ3": "What happens when I delete my account?",
  "trustFaqA3": "When you confirm deletion in Privacy Center, we immediately remove your Firestore profile, cloud backups, chat history, and community content from our servers, then delete your Firebase Authentication account. Local data on your device remains until you uninstall the app. Technical backups at Firebase may be retained briefly per their infrastructure policies.",
  "trustFaqQ4": "Is AI chat private?",
  "trustFaqA4": "AI chat requires Premium. Guest users keep chat on the device only. Registered Premium users may have messages stored in the cloud to restore conversations. Every AI message is sent to Google Gemini and/or DeepSeek for processing — see our Privacy Policy. We recommend not sharing information you would not want a third-party AI provider to process.",
  "trustFaqQ5": "Can I use Lune without an account?",
  "trustFaqA5": "Yes. You can use Lune as a guest with an anonymous Firebase account linked to your device — no email required. Core cycle tracking works fully offline. Cloud backup, Premium AI, cross-device chat history, and some community features require a registered account.",
  "trustFaqQ6": "Where is my data stored?",
  "trustFaqA6": "Locally on your phone by default in an AES-256 encrypted database. If you enable Premium cloud backup, encrypted backup payloads are stored in Google Firebase, which may process data in the United States and other regions.",
  "trustFaqQ7": "How do I export my data?",
  "trustFaqA7": "Open Privacy Center → Export Data to copy an encrypted local backup to your clipboard. You can save it in a password manager or secure notes app. For help with portability requests, email merrsoheb@gmail.com.",
  "trustFaqQ8": "How do I contact you about privacy?",
  "trustFaqA8": "Email merrsoheb@gmail.com or use Contact Support in Privacy Center. We aim to respond to privacy requests within 30 days.",
  "trustFaqQ9": "Is AI chat free?",
  "trustFaqA9": "No. Lune AI is a Premium feature. Premium subscribers can send up to 30 AI messages per calendar day — enforced on our servers. If a provider fails, we do not count that message against your limit.",
  "trustFaqQ10": "What does Premium unlock?",
  "trustFaqA10": "Premium includes cloud cycle backup, Lune AI chat (30 messages/day), and attaching photos or videos in community posts and stories. Core local tracking remains free for all users.",
  "trustFaqQ11": "How does Stealth mode work?",
  "trustFaqA11": "Stealth mode shows a calculator screen instead of Lune until you enter your secret PIN and press equals. It protects your privacy if someone opens your phone. It is a local disguise only — enable it in Privacy Center.",
  "trustFaqQ12": "Who sees my community posts?",
  "trustFaqA12": "Posts are visible to members of the Lune communities you join. You can report unsafe content; reported posts may be auto-hidden while we review them. Community participation is optional and requires consent.",
  "trustFaqQ13": "Can I share a health report with my doctor?",
  "trustFaqA13": "Yes. Lune can generate a health summary report from your logged data that you can review and share yourself. We do not send reports to doctors automatically — you choose what to share and with whom.",
  "trustFaqQ14": "Does the magazine use my personal data?",
  "trustFaqA14": "No. Educational articles in the Lune magazine are editorial content managed separately from your private cycle logs. Reading articles does not upload your personal health data for personalization.",
  "trustFaqQ15": "What notifications does Lune send?",
  "trustFaqA15": "If you opt in, we may send cycle reminders, wellness prompts, and important app updates via Firebase Cloud Messaging. We do not send promotional ads or sell notification audiences to third parties. You can disable notifications in device settings.",
  "trustFaqQ16": "What are my GDPR rights?",
  "trustFaqA16": "If you are in the EEA or UK, you may request access, correction, deletion, or export of your personal data. Delete your account in Privacy Center for immediate server removal, or email merrsoheb@gmail.com for assistance. We respond within 30 days.",
  "trustFaqQ17": "What Android permissions does Lune use?",
  "trustFaqA17": "Internet for sign-in and optional online features; Notifications for reminders you enable; Google Play Billing for Premium; exact alarms and boot restart for reliable local reminders. Photos or videos are requested only when you attach media in community (Premium) or choose a profile photo. We do not access your contacts, SMS, or call logs.",
  "trustFaqQ18": "How do Google Play subscriptions work?",
  "trustFaqA18": "Premium is billed through Google Play. Subscriptions auto-renew unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the period ends. Manage or cancel in Google Play → Subscriptions. Refunds follow Google Play's refund policy. Deleting your Lune account does not automatically stop billing — cancel the subscription separately.",
  "trustFaqQ19": "What is the minimum age to use Lune?",
  "trustFaqA19": "You must be at least 13 years old. Users under 13 cannot continue after the age gate. Some community features are restricted to users 18 and older. Parents who believe a child under 13 used Lune should contact us to request deletion.",
  "trustFaqQ20": "Is Lune a medical device or medical advice?",
  "trustFaqA20": "No. Lune is for informational wellness tracking only — not a medical device, diagnosis, or treatment. Cycle predictions, AI chat, community posts, and magazine articles are not medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional for medical decisions.",
  "trustFaqQ21": "What data does Lune collect (Google Play Data Safety)?",
  "trustFaqA21": "Data you provide: cycle dates, symptoms, moods, wellness notes, and optional community posts. Account data if registered (email, name, sign-in method). Technical data: device tokens for notifications, anonymized crash reports, and approximate activity timestamps. Premium AI messages are sent to Google Gemini/DeepSeek for processing. Data is not sold. Core tracking stays on your device unless you enable Premium cloud backup.",

  "trustBodyDataTitle": "Your Body, Your Data",
  "trustBodyDataIntro": "Your menstrual and wellness data is deeply personal. At Lune, you are in control — always. This page explains what you log, who owns it, and how optional features use it.",
  "trustBodyDataS1Title": "Ownership",
  "trustBodyDataS1Body": "You own the cycle, symptom, mood, flow, water intake, and wellness data you log. Lune is a tool to help you understand your body — not a platform that monetizes your health information or sells insights about you.",
  "trustBodyDataS2Title": "Local-first design",
  "trustBodyDataS2Body": "The app works fully offline. Your daily logs are written to an encrypted database on your device first. Nothing leaves your phone unless you choose cloud backup, AI chat, community, or other features that require a network connection.",
  "trustBodyDataS3Title": "Explicit consent",
  "trustBodyDataS3Body": "Cloud backup, AI features, community participation, and push notifications each require separate consent in Privacy Center. You can enable or disable them individually without losing your local cycle history.",
  "trustBodyDataS4Title": "No hidden sharing",
  "trustBodyDataS4Body": "We do not share your cycle data with employers, insurers, advertisers, or external social networks. Community posts and stories are visible only within Lune communities you choose to join.",
  "trustBodyDataS5Title": "What you can log",
  "trustBodyDataS5Body": "Lune lets you track periods, symptoms, moods, pain levels, water intake, and other wellness notes you choose to record. You decide how much detail to add each day. None of this is required beyond what you need for your own understanding.",
  "trustBodyDataS6Title": "How AI uses your cycle context",
  "trustBodyDataS6Body": "When you use Lune AI (Premium), relevant cycle context you approve may be sent to our servers and then to Google Gemini or DeepSeek to personalize responses. AI is optional — you can track your cycle without ever opening chat.",
  "trustBodyDataS7Title": "Magazine & education",
  "trustBodyDataS7Body": "Articles in the Lune magazine are general health education content. They are separate from your private logs and are not generated from your personal cycle data. Editors publish articles through our admin tools — not by reading your diary.",
  "trustBodyDataS8Title": "Portability",
  "trustBodyDataS8Body": "You can export an encrypted backup from Privacy Center at any time. Your data belongs to you — if you leave Lune, you can take a copy with you before deleting your account.",

  "trustDataEndsTitle": "Your Data Ends With You",
  "trustDataEndsIntro": "When you decide to leave Lune, your data should leave too. This page walks through every step — server deletion, local files, subscriptions, and what cannot be undone.",
  "trustDataEndsS1Title": "Delete anytime",
  "trustDataEndsS1Body": "You can delete your account from Privacy Center at any time. No phone calls, no dark patterns — just a clear confirmation step. Guest users can clear local data by uninstalling the app.",
  "trustDataEndsS2Title": "Immediate server deletion",
  "trustDataEndsS2Body": "When you confirm account deletion, our servers immediately remove your Firestore profile, cloud cycle backups, chat history, and community posts, then delete your Firebase Authentication account. This is not a 30-day waiting period — deletion starts right away.",
  "trustDataEndsS3Title": "Local data",
  "trustDataEndsS3Body": "Data on your device is not automatically erased when you delete your cloud account. Uninstall the app or use your phone's app settings to remove remaining local encrypted databases and preferences.",
  "trustDataEndsS4Title": "Backups you exported",
  "trustDataEndsS4Body": "If you exported a backup file to your clipboard or saved it elsewhere, that copy is outside our control. Delete those files if you no longer need them — we cannot reach into your notes app or cloud drive.",
  "trustDataEndsS5Title": "Permanent action",
  "trustDataEndsS5Body": "Account deletion cannot be undone. If you return to Lune later, you start fresh unless you restore from a local backup you saved before deleting.",
  "trustDataEndsS6Title": "Guest vs registered accounts",
  "trustDataEndsS6Body": "Guest accounts exist mainly on your device with a lightweight anonymous Firebase identity. Deleting a registered account triggers full server cleanup. Guests should uninstall the app to remove all local traces.",
  "trustDataEndsS7Title": "Premium subscriptions",
  "trustDataEndsS7Body": "Deleting your Lune account does not automatically cancel a Google Play subscription. Open Google Play → Subscriptions to cancel Premium billing separately so you are not charged after leaving.",
  "trustDataEndsS8Title": "Community content removal",
  "trustDataEndsS8Body": "When you delete your account, we remove your posts, comments, and stories from Lune communities through automated server cleanup. Remaining copies in other users' caches disappear as they refresh or reinstall.",

  "trustA11yTitle": "Accessibility at Lune",
  "trustA11yIntro": "We believe everyone deserves access to cycle health tools — regardless of language, vision, or motor ability. Accessibility is an ongoing commitment, not a one-time feature.",
  "trustA11yS1Title": "Our commitment",
  "trustA11yS1Body": "We design Lune to be usable with screen readers, system font scaling, and both left-to-right and right-to-left layouts. Arabic and English receive equal attention in navigation, labels, and reading direction.",
  "trustA11yS2Title": "In-app features",
  "trustA11yS2Body": "Lune respects your device's text size, bold text, and contrast settings where supported by Flutter and your operating system. Navigation uses standard Material patterns for predictable screen-reader behavior across tabs and forms.",
  "trustA11yS3Title": "Request accommodations",
  "trustA11yS3Body": "If you encounter a barrier while using Lune, email merrsoheb@gmail.com with a description of the issue, your device model, and your preferred language. We take accessibility feedback seriously and prioritize fixes that block core tracking.",
  "trustA11yS4Title": "Ongoing improvements",
  "trustA11yS4Body": "We review new features for color contrast, touch target size, and screen reader labels before release. Past releases have improved RTL layouts, larger tap areas, and clearer error messages — and more improvements are planned.",
  "trustA11yS5Title": "Arabic & English parity",
  "trustA11yS5Body": "Switching between Arabic and English flips the entire interface direction — menus, cards, and legal pages included. You should not need to fight the layout to read content in your language.",
  "trustA11yS6Title": "Themes & system settings",
  "trustA11yS6Body": "Lune follows your device theme where possible and uses readable typography across light backgrounds. If system high-contrast mode is enabled, OS-level settings may further improve readability.",
  "trustA11yS7Title": "Roadmap",
  "trustA11yS7Body": "We are working toward broader WCAG-aligned improvements — including richer screen reader descriptions for charts, keyboard navigation enhancements, and user-tested contrast audits. Tell us what matters most to you."
}
